+// Pattern letters whose output needs no locale text: their counts as Java accepts them (and a
+// few counts it refuses), so that acceptance, output and parsing are all compared.
+// (Text letters - G, E, a, B, z, O, MMM and up, QQQ and up - and the localized week letters w W Y
+// e c need @js-joda/locale, and are left out; N and A stay under 2^53.)
+// (DD, nn.., NN.., AA.. and F: TestHegelMinWidthPatternLettersAgreeWithJava)
